<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Elders (Somaliland)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1993">1993</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Guurti</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Guurti, or House of Elders, is the upper chamber of the parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, made up of clan elders and their representatives. Councils of elders mediated in the conferences that ended Somaliland's internal conflicts, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borama">Borama</a> conference of 1993 gave them a formal place in the state. The house reviews legislation and has repeatedly extended the terms of elected bodies when elections were delayed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-elders-somaliland.jpg" alt="House of Elders (Somaliland)" width="320" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Somaliland House of Elders Golaha Guurtidda JSL Vector: Siirski · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_the_Somaliland_House_of_Elders.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
